        "1/f = 1/u - 1/v"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "1/f = 1/v - 1/u",
      "explanation": "The lens formula relates the focal length (f) of a lens to the image distance (v) and the object distance (u)."
    },
    {
      "question": "How is magnification (m) of a lens defined?",
      "options": [
        "m = u/v",
        "m = v * u",
        "m = v/u",
        "m = u - v"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "m = v/u",
      "explanation": "Magnification describes how large or small the image is relative to the object, calculated as the ratio of image distance to object distance."
    },
