    "bullets": [
      "DNA utilizes specific base pairing rules to maintain genetic stability.",
      "Adenine (A) always pairs with Thymine (T).",
      "Guanine (G) always pairs with Cytosine (C)."
    ]
  },
  {
    "slide_title": "Semiconservative DNA Replication",
    "bullets": [
      "DNA replication follows a semiconservative model.",
      "Each original DNA strand serves as a template for a new complementary strand.",
      "The resulting DNA molecules consist of one original strand and one newly synthesized strand."
    ]
  },
  {
    "slide_title": "Protein Synthesis: Transcription and Translation",
    "bullets": [
      "Genetic information is transcribed from DNA into messenger RNA (mRNA).",
      "mRNA acts as a mobile carrier of the genetic code.",
